both custom-made and ready-made websites can add your CKD application. The method is slightly different.


| Website Type            | Can Add CKD App? | How                                                             |
| ----------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Custom-made website** | ✅ Yes            | Integrate directly with the code or embed the app using its URL |
| **Ready-made website**  | ✅ Yes            | Add the public URL using an iframe/embed block                  |


Simple idea
                    CKD Flask Application
                           │
                    Public URL
                           │
              ┌────────────┴────────────┐
              ↓                         ↓
       Custom Website             Ready-made Website
       HTML/CSS/JS                WordPress/Elementor
              ↓                         ↓
       Direct Integration            iframe
              ↓                         ↓
            User                      User

So the main requirement is:

Your Flask CKD application must be deployed and have a public URL.

Then it can be connected to both types of websites.

Both website types can use the same deployed Flask app, but the integration differs: 
custom sites can connect through direct API requests instead of an iframe, while ready-made sites usually embed the public app URL.

